From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomas Mihalicka <tomas@mihalicka.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] Trace requests and export payment metrics

When a charge went wrong there was no trace of it: retries happened
silently, and a 500 said nothing about its cause.

Log through tracing, at the level set by PAYMENTS_LOG_LEVEL. Each
failed charge attempt is logged with its attempt number and operation
key, a charge that ends unknown is logged as an error, and each
payment's outcome is logged in a span that carries its tenant. An
internal error is logged in full before the client gets a generic 500.

GET /metrics exports counters for created payments and for charge
outcomes, so an operator can alert when unknown outcomes climb.

Areas: observability
